  "decision": "The ternary. Its condition is an ArgumentMember and both branches are ArgumentExpressionMembers, which is not decoration: an ArgumentExpression wraps its value in an OwnedExpressionReference, so the branches are referenced rather than evaluated in place. That is how a conditional evaluates only the branch it takes, and it is visible in the grammar rather than left to semantics.",
